      "dom_id": "question-93124",
      "problem": "A tank with a capacity of $2\\,000$ liters is filled with $1\\,400$ liters of water. What percentage of the tank is filled with water?",
      "worked_solution": "We're given a part and a whole, and we must find a percentage. So, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{percentage}=\\text{part}÷\\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn this case, \n\n- the part is the amount of water, which is $1\\,400$ liters, and\n\n- the whole is the capacity of the tank, which is $2\\,000$ liters.\n\nSubstituting our numbers into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{percentage}=1\\,400÷2\\,000=\\frac{14}{20}.\n$$\n\nTo write this as a percentage, we create an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{20}=\\frac{14\\times 5}{20\\times 5}=\\frac{70}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{70}{100}=70%\n$$\n\nTherefore, $70%$ of the tank is filled with water.",
      "result": "Incorrect",
